-- title:
--   Ring homomorphisms on the weight-2 Hecke algebra are determined by the T_ℓ
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and $S \subseteq \mathbb{N}$ a set of naturals such that every prime $q$ dividing $N$ belongs to $S$. Write $\mathbb{T} =$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) for the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the set consisting of the operators `heckeTLin 2` attached to primes $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \notin S$, together with the operators `heckeULin` attached to primes $q$ with $q \mid N$ and $q \notin S$, where `heckeTLin k hp hpN` is the $\mathbb{C}$-linear endomorphism of $S_k(\Gamma_0(N))$ induced by the $q$-expansion-level Hecke operator `heckeT k p`. Let $R$ be a commutative ring and let $\theta_1, \theta_2 \colon \mathbb{T} \to R$ be ring homomorphisms. Assume that for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \notin S$ the two homomorphisms agree on the element [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.T`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L77) of $\mathbb{T}$ determined by $\ell$, namely $\mathrm{heckeTLin}\,2$ for that $\ell$ viewed as an element of the subalgebra. Then $\theta_1 = \theta_2$.
--
--   This is the extensionality statement for characters (more generally, for ring-valued homomorphisms) of the anaemic weight-$2$ Hecke algebra away from $S$: under the hypothesis that $S$ contains all prime factors of $N$, no $U_q$ generator survives, so the $T_\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$ already generate. It is used to identify systems of Hecke eigenvalues, and is cited in the construction of algebra homomorphisms out of localised Hecke algebras in the level-lowering and degeneracy-map arguments.
-- source:
